# Everything in the repository is stored with LF, and checked out with LF on
# every platform. Left to itself, Git for Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, which is fine for source and not fine for anything compared byte
# for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The embedded fixtures are exactly that case. Tests read them off disk, hand
# them to the macros, and assert on the bytes that come back, so a fixture has
# to arrive as it was committed. Marking them binary keeps every conversion,
# present and future, away from them.
crates/embark/tests/assets/** -text
crates/embark/tests/fixtures/** -text
crates/embark/examples/assets/** -text
